================================================================================
(2)+(3) each family's M is achieved at argq; band-edge ceil(q/14)/q DECREASES in q
================================================================================
  family                                     M  argq ceil(argq/14)/argq qmin_clear
  AP {1..13} (tight, non-DC)              1/14    14       1/14=0.0714       None
  GW {1..11,13,24} (tight, non-DC)        1/14    14       1/14=0.0714       None
  kps 2-block {1,2,3,4,10..18}            1/12    24       1/12=0.0833         24
  compressed 2*{1..12}u{13}               1/13    26       1/13=0.0769         26
  deep well {1..12,182}                 14/183   183     14/183=0.0765         27
  => the DEEP WELL achieves M at a LARGE argq (183); kps's 2-block at SMALL argq (24).
     Since ceil(q/14)/q decreases in q, the LARGE-argq family (deep well) has the SMALLEST M.

